From: Mark Adler <madler@alumni.caltech.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid compiler complaints if _TIME_BITS defined when building zlib

gzguts.h undefines _FILE_OFFSET_BITS whenever _LARGEFILE64_SOURCE is set,
and glibc rejects that pair once _TIME_BITS is 64:

    features-time64.h:26:5: error: "_TIME_BITS=64 is allowed only with
    _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64"

oe-core puts both flags in TARGET_CC_ARCH for 32-bit arm, so the four gz*.c
files fail to compile for any 32-bit target. zlib does not use time_t, so
dropping _TIME_BITS along with _FILE_OFFSET_BITS is the whole fix.

In zlib since v1.3. The SDK pins v1.2.11, the revision
cmake/external/zlib.cmake names, so this is backported rather than the pin
moved.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/a566e156b3fa07b566ddbf6801b517a9dba04fa3]
Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
--- a/gzguts.h
+++ b/gzguts.h
@@ -7,9 +7,8 @@
 #  ifndef _LARGEFILE_SOURCE
 #    define _LARGEFILE_SOURCE 1
 #  endif
-#  ifdef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
-#    undef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
-#  endif
+#  undef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+#  undef _TIME_BITS
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_HIDDEN
